    per-galaxy spread sd(log a_0) = 0.663 dex, MAD = 0.485 dex
    restricted to the |LAMBDA| <= 1.5 gate (N = 27): a_0 = 8.274e-11 (+-0.187 dex)  =  canonical -0.054 / alt -0.135 dex
    LOCAL rung, identical per-object inversion at each SPARC galaxy's lowest-acceleration point (N = 125): a_0 = 9.634e-11 (+-0.024 dex) = canonical +0.013 / alt -0.069 dex
    ==> log a_0(z ~ 1.03) - log a_0(z ~ 0) = +0.058 +- 0.125 dex (statistical only)
  [PASS] k03-2 THE MEASUREMENT: a_0 read at z ~ 1 in the deep-MOND regime and at z ~ 0 with the identical per-object estimator.  The check that can fail is that the two agree within their statistical errors   (z ~ 1: 1.102e-10; z ~ 0: 9.634e-11; difference +0.058 +- 0.125 dex (0.47 sigma))

